# Auto-deploy to Vercel production

After every substantive code change in this repo, deploy to Vercel production
without asking for confirmation. The user has standing approval.

## When to deploy

- After finishing a coherent unit of work that affects the running app
  (UI tweaks, API/server changes, config edits, dependency bumps, etc.)
- After a successful `npm run deploy:prod` (build must pass before Vercel runs)
- Skip for purely no-op changes (whitespace-only, comments, README copy)

## How to deploy

Run **one** command (do not split into separate build + deploy shell calls):

```bash
npm run deploy:prod
```

- This runs `npm run build` then `vercel --prod --yes` in a single approval
- Use the global Vercel CLI; do not use `npx vercel`
- Run from the repo root (already linked to project
  `jesses-projects-cb5ea703/maroma-staging-isolated`)
- Tail the last ~20 lines of output to capture the deployment URL and inspect URL
- Report the production URL, deployment URL, and inspect URL back to the user

## Notes

- The project no longer uses `vercel.json`; framework detection comes from
  Project Settings (Next.js)
- Only deploy on behalf of the user — do not push or amend git commits unless
  explicitly asked
